\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Beneath the Cross of Jesus
\par I fain will take my stand-
\par The shadow of the mighty rock
\par Within a weary land;
\par Ahome within the wilderness,
\par A rest upon the way,
\par From the burning of the noontide heat
\par And the burden of the day. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2 upon the Cross of Jesus 
\par My eyes at times can see
\par The very dying form of One
\par Who suffered there for me.
\par And from my stricken heart, with, tears,
\par Two wonders I confess-
\par The wonders of the redeeming love,
\par And my own worthlessness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3 I take, O Cross, thy shadow,
\par For my abiding-place!
\par I ask no other sunshine than
\par The sunshine of His face;
\par Content to let the world go by,
\par To know no gain nor loss-
\par My sinful self my only shame,
\par My glory all-the Cross.  
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
